A Linux-style page exercises both conversion directions, metadata and selections.
-- input.1 --
.TH TOOL 1 "2026-10-21" "Example tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tool \- inspect pages
.SH DESCRIPTION
Plain
.B bold
.I italic
and ordinary text.
.br
A second line.
.SS DETAIL
.TP 8
.B --flag
A definition.
.RS 2
Indented text.
.RE
.TP
.B --other
Another definition.
.PP
A safe
.UR https://example.com/docs?q=a&b=c
link
.UE .
See
.MR printf 3 ,
then
.SM small.
.EX
  tool --flag

    indented
.EE
-- case.json --
{"equivalent":true}
-- expected.1 --
.TH "TOOL" "1" "2026-10-21" "Example tools" "User Commands"
.SH "\f[B]NAME\f[R]"
.PP
\&\f[R]tool - inspect pages\f[R]\c
.SH "\f[B]DESCRIPTION\f[R]"
.PP
\&\f[R]Plain \f[R]\c
\&\f[B]bold\f[R]\c
\&\f[R] \f[R]\c
\&\f[I]italic\f[R]\c
\&\f[R] and ordinary text.\f[R]\c
.br
\&\f[R]A second line.\f[R]\c
.SS "\f[B]DETAIL\f[R]"
.PP
.TP "8"
\&\f[B]--flag\f[R]

\&\f[R]A definition.\f[R]\c
.RS "2"
.PP
\&\f[R]Indented text.\f[R]\c
.RE
.TP "8"
\&\f[B]--other\f[R]

\&\f[R]Another definition.\f[R]\c
.PP
\&\f[R]A safe \f[R]\c
.UR "https://example.com/docs?q=a&b=c"
\&\f[R]link\f[R]\c
.UE
\&\f[R]. See \f[R]\c
.ft R
.MR "printf" "3" "\c"
.ft R
\&\f[R], then \f[R]\c
.SM "\&\f[R]small.\f[R]\c"
.nf
\&\f[CR]  tool --flag\f[R]\c


\&\f[CR]    indented\f[R]\c

.fi
